---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <main class="flex flex-col w-full justify-center items-center">
    <div class="w-1/2 flex flex-col gap-10">
      <h1 class="text-4xl">Our Purpose</h1>
      <p>
        In the modern age of technology, the internet is what keeps people
        connected to the news, education, world politics and family members.
        Internet speed is something that we should not worry about, especially
        in a first world country, and being the leader in technological
        advancement. Unfortunately, the truth is that companies not only
        restrict internet speed, but also charge a premium for higher internet
        speeds, effectively isolating communities where companies refuse to
        develop the infrastructure to support them. Lower internet speeds mean
        less access to the internet. Families either take turns using the
        internet or don’t use them completely which for families who have
        children in school, could prove detrimental to their grades. This issue
        was not brought into the light up until covid-19 pandemic forced
        everyone to quarantine at home. Students from across the country, from
        communities of color, to impoverished counties, all struggle to keep
        their kids engaged in school. Recent studies show that not only adults,
        but families with children are stuck, without the ability to afford
        reliable broadband, leaving many students from low-income communities
        stranded and at an education and economical disadvantage.
        <br />
        <pre>
                [ THE DIGITAL DIVIDE ]
      
      HIGH-PROFIT AREA           LOW-PROFIT AREA
      (Tier 1 Fiber)             (Throttled/Legacy)
      ________________           ________________
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|         |                |
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|         |      ....      |
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|         |     .    .     |
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|  &lt;&lt;&lt;&lt;   |    .      .    |
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|  [VS]   |   .        .   |
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|  &gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;   |    .      .    |
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|         |     .    .     |
     |@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@|         |      ....      |
     |________________|         |________________|
      
       1GBPS UNLIMITED            25MBPS CAPPED
          [FAST]                    [SLOW]
        </pre>
        <br />
        I believe that since the infrastructure for the internet is already in place
        and the cost of maintaining it is not high, I believe that the government
        should step in and regulate the internet to ensure that everyone has access
        to it. The internet is a necessity in today’s world, and it should be treated
        as such. It is not fair that some people have access to high-speed internet
        while others do not. This is a problem that needs to be addressed, and I believe
        that the government has a responsibility to ensure that everyone has access
        to the internet.
        <br /><br />
        Companies should not be limited as well. The internet is a place for innovation
        and creativity, and it should be a level playing field for all companies.
        ISPs should not be able to discriminate against certain companies or websites,
        and they should not be able to charge extra for increased speeds their content
        are served.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-row gap-5">
        <a
          href="/videos"
          class="px-4 py-2 border border-black hover:bg-black hover:text-white transition rounded"
          >Videos</a
        >
        <a
          href="/research"
          class="px-4 py-2 border border-black hover:bg-black hover:text-white transition rounded"
          >Research</a
        >
        <p class="text-center">---></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>
